-- title:
--   Fine moduli package for Γ₀(N)-kernels and a linked Γ₁(ℓ)-point
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a Noetherian commutative ring, $\ell$ a prime with $5\le\ell$, and $N$ a nonzero natural number whose image in $A$, like that of $\ell$, is a unit. Three transport hypotheses are assumed, each for all $A$-algebras $T$: that `IsGamma1Point` for $(W,\ell,D)$ — the point $(D.xP,D.yP)$ satisfies the affine Weierstrass equation of $W$, $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_\ell$ vanishes at $D.xP$, and $(D.xQ,D.yQ)=(D.xP,D.yP)$ — is preserved by a change of variables $C$, the datum being moved by `LevelPData.variableChange`; that `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` is preserved when $h$ is replaced by `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h`; and that a divisibility $h \mid$ `inLineMulPoly W ℓ n x` is carried by $C$ to `kernelVariableChangeDeg C d h` $\mid$ `inLineMulPoly (C • W) ℓ n (u⁻¹² (x - r))`. Form the level component that assigns to $T$ a family $(h_p)_{p\mid N}$ of polynomials with `IsGamma0PowAt W p (N.factorization p) (h_p)`, a `LevelPData` which is a $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-point, and a trivial third slot, restricted by the link condition `IsGamma1Link`: if $\ell \mid N$ then $h_\ell$ divides `inLineMulPoly W ℓ (ℓ ^ (N.factorization ℓ - 1)) D.xP`. Passing to the associated rigid Weierstrass data (curves with unit discriminant carrying such a level structure) and to the moduli datum of these data modulo changes of variables, with $j$-invariant, the assertion is that there exists a `LevelModuliPackageAbs A` for it, that is, an $A$-algebra $B_0$ together with a point `univ` over $B_0$ such that every point over any $A$-algebra $T$ is `D.map φ univ` for a unique $A$-algebra map $\varphi : B_0 \to T$, which moreover is of finite type over $A$ and integral over the $A$-subalgebra of $B_0$ generated by `P.j₀`.
--
--   This is the existence of a fine moduli scheme, in affine coordinate-ring form, for elliptic curves equipped with a $\Gamma_0(N)$-structure given by generators of cyclic kernels at each prime power dividing $N$ together with a $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-point linked to the $\ell$-part of that structure, over an arbitrary Noetherian base in which $\ell N$ is invertible. It is the input for the subsequent analysis of the resulting algebra at maximal ideals and for its comparison with power series rings via $q$-expansions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_Diamond_exists_levelModuliPackageAbs_trivial_rigidDataH1Pow.lean

